ical_concept_only","flags":["The key counts simultaneous arrivals at a pool end as passing. If 'pass each other' requires crossing in the interior, the result is 16, which is absent from the choices.","The wording does not specify whether simultaneous arrival at a pool end counts as passing. Choice C matches the all-meetings interpretation; strict interior passing yields an unlisted answer.","In the modular route, the supplied integer-congruence scope applies to integer event indices, not directly to an arbitrary real-valued time variable.","confirmed_answer_ambiguity"],"questionId":"1960_AMC_12_Q34","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"repeat-one-motion-cycle","label":"Count one motion cycle","methodDirectNodeIds":{"repeat-one-motion-cycle":["cnm_p111","cnm_030"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p111","cnm_030"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 10 rows","reason":"For n rows, the bottom row has 2n - 1 cans. The total is n(1 + 2n - 1)/2 = n^2. Since n^2 = 100 and n is positive, n = 10.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2004_AMC_10B_Q10","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_030","cnm_075"],"id":"pair-row-sums","label":"Add the row sizes in opposite orders","methodDirectNodeIds":{"pair-row-sums":["cnm_h204"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h204","cnm_030","cnm_075"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 16,089","reason":"The composition is h₁(x)=10x-1. Starting from 1 gives 9,89,889,... . In general hₙ(1)=(8·10ⁿ+1)/9, which has n-1 digits equal to 8 followed by 9. The requested digit sum is 2010·8+9=16,089.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2011_AMC_12B_Q17","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"id":"decimal-pattern","label":"Follow the decimal recurrence","nodeIds":["cnm_030"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_h048","ma